# Section layout refactor (default workflow)

When asked to refactor, redesign, or replace a **page section**, follow this unless the user opts out.

## Non-negotiables

- **Compliance gate**: `.cursor/rules/design-compliance-preflight.mdc` (band rhythm, layout roots, contrast, targeted DESIGN-SYSTEM reads)—pass before calling the refactor done.
- **Styling**: `DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` tokens and classes in `glc-site/src/styles/glc-base.css`—no Tailwind utilities on components (repo standard).
- **Section uniqueness (per page)**: A section is **unique** — it must not appear twice on the same page. That means **one** top-level instance per distinct `id`/anchor, **and** the same *layout pattern* (same band/split/grid DNA) must not be reused; add a variant or consolidate. Large copy needs tabs, accordion, columns, or progressive disclosure—not a wall of text.
- **Parallax budget**: At most **one** animated parallax stack **per page** among **C3**, **D7**, or hero **A1/A2** polygon stacks. If the page already uses one, use static motifs or B-slots here.
- **B-slot décor**: Empty decorative nodes only; `aria-hidden="true"`; parent is `position: relative`.

## DNA (inspiration, not cloning)

- Open `section-dna/approved-sections.json` and cite **2–3** `sections[].id` whose `visualDna` and `layersBottomToTop` match the section’s **job** (band, split, grid, CTA, etc.).
- The shipped layout must be **new**: distinct grid/asymmetry and a **new class prefix**—not a copy of a cited id.

## Motifs (canonical set only)

- Pick from **DESIGN-SYSTEM.md** → **Production primitives (21 motif IDs)** — table lists Shell (`.dse`, `.ls`, grain, …), **A1–A6**, **B1–B5**, **C1–C3**, **D1–D7**, type watermark.
- State **motif ID + concrete class names** and **one-sentence rationale** (e.g. D1 for clipped media, A3 for light↔dark seam, D6 for split seam).
- Respect **globalDnaDraft** / **conflictsToEliminate** in `approved-sections.json` when touching shared `#id` CSS.

## Reusable chat prompt (fill the brackets)

```
Goal: Refactor [section name] on [page/route] — outcome: [what should feel/be different].

Hard constraints: DESIGN-SYSTEM.md + glc-base.css only; section layout uniqueness on this page; one parallax stack max (C3/D7/hero A1–A2) site-wide for this page; B-slots aria-hidden.

DNA: From section-dna/approved-sections.json, use inspiration from ids [id1], [id2], [id3] — deliver a NEW layout + new class prefix, not a duplicate.

Motif: Chosen ID(s) from the 21-motif table in DESIGN-SYSTEM.md + shell classes; justify in one sentence.

Deliver: (1) IA eyebrow→headline→support→CTA (2) layout/asymmetry sketch (3) motif + z-order (4) files: TSX, content JSON if needed, glc-base.css block with anchor comment.
```

**Optional:** Paste this block into a Cursor **Notepad** and `@`-mention it in Agent/Chat for a one-click “load the whole prompt.”
